{"diagnosis": "Fetch test uses 256-word NOP mem (ADDI x0,x0,0, opcode 0010011) expecting progress with no trap, but trace shows TRAP: cpu trap asserted and tohost: FAIL 0xdead. Expected is_alu_reg_imm=1 for 0010011, but excerpt line 877 decodes is_alu_reg_imm as 7'b0010111 (AUIPC opcode), so NOP is not recognized as legal ALU-imm and traps. Root cause is wrong opcode constant on line 877 duplicating AUIPC instead of OP-IMM 0010011.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -874,7 +874,7 @@
 			is_beq_bne_blt_bge_bltu_bgeu <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b1100011;
 			is_lb_lh_lw_lbu_lhu          <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0000011;
 			is_sb_sh_sw                  <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0100011;
-			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010111;
+			is_alu_reg_imm               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0010011;
 			is_alu_reg_reg               <= mem_rdata_latched[6:0] == 7'b0110011;

 			{ decoded_imm_j[31:20], decoded_imm_j[10:1], decoded_imm_j[11], decoded_imm_j[19:12], decoded_imm_j[0] } <= $signed({mem_rdata_latched[31:12], 1'b0});", "expected": "tohost: PASS with no TRAP: cpu trap asserted"}

